(7566619, 1213788, 109363, '<td valign="top">thanks so much for the comments.<br/> <br/>this was almost a fool the viewer redux... this is the top of a deer skull, close up on the bone plate fusion zones.  it was a younger deer, so the fusions were no complete and fading.  call it skull-techtonics ;-)<br/> <br/>i believe the dendritic river-like features towards the edges are part lf the sinus/nasal drainage architecture, since they were associated with cavities, which i cropped off.<br/> <br/>and the slight discoloration and few hairs did their part to give it an earthly look.</td>', 'thanks so much for the comments. this was almost a fool the viewer redux... this is the top of a deer skull, close up on the bone plate fusion zones.  it was a younger deer, so the fusions were no complete and fading.  call it skull-techtonics ;-) i believe the dendritic river-like features towards the edges are part lf the sinus/nasal drainage architecture, since they were associated with cavities, which i cropped off. and the slight discoloration and few hairs did their part to give it an earthly look.', '2018-04-20 07:36:21.000000', NULL, 0),
